  "description": "No bike can truly “do it all,” but these come darn close. A cross bike is always on cyclists lists of “if I could only own one bike…” This is my “if I could only own one bike” bike.\n\nThe steel used in the cross frame is a heat-treated, double butted, 4130 chrome-moly tubing that comes from the leading steel tubing supplier in Taiwan. It’s tubing I specified for the ride quality I want.\n\nThe V6.1 frame differs from previous generations with a new fork crown from Long Shen – same twin plate style aesthetics with a bit more tire clearance. Other features include clearance for up to 50 millimeters of rubber and horizontal dropouts to fine-tune chainstay length or run it as a single-speed.",
